WEBVTT

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:14.130
"Construction Area
Keep Out"

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:17.640
I've got this!

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:35.780
I'm exhausted.
Isn't it about time for a nap?

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:50.000
I told you to stay back!

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.510
You just need to keep the Others at bay.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:54.170
Y-Yes, sir.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:56.680
We're sorry, Commander Shiden.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:01.720
Well done, Commander Shiden.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:04.930
You should try slacking off for once,
Commander Shiden.

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:06.810
Shut it.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:11.020
I always thought I'd make
commander someday, but...

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:15.070
Training new recruits and looking
after each platoon member.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:17.450
Such is a commander's role.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:21.120
Kasane was supposed to
keep serving as commander.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.580
Would you like her to resume her duties?

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:24.750
No way!

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:29.330
Plus, she already has another assignment.
It's too late now.

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:30.880
What did I miss?

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:32.500
What are you doing here?

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:34.960
Weren't you needed elsewhere?

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:39.720
I came to give you a progress report,
but then I heard my name mentioned.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:41.180
Never mind that.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:44.930
We were talking about what a
great job I'm doing as commander.

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:47.140
"Arriving in 5 minutes"

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.270
You have plans?

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:51.310
Yuito's coming, too.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:53.270
I'll go meet him.

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:06.540
Thanks.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:13.630
It's been a while, Kasane.

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:15.050
Long time, no see.

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:16.720
You look well.

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:49.180
"To Each Their Own Future"

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:52.770
"To Each Their Own Future"
I don't need it anymore,
but they told me to take it easy.

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:55.400
You should listen to your doctor.

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.280
So you really did volunteer.

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:01.610
Yes.

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:04.450
Where's Arashi?

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:06.910
She said it was too noisy to nap here.

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:09.950
So you're here to start
the discharge process.

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:12.210
I also wanted to say hi to everyone.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:14.330
--I'm so tired.
--Me, too.

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:17.130
So many new faces.

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:20.210
There's been a flood of new recruits.

00:04:20.210 --> 00:04:24.880
Well, the Extinction Belt may be gone,
but there are still Others to deal with.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:27.720
Shiden, I hear you were
promoted to commander.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:28.850
Can you handle it?

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:30.520
Of course, I can.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:34.440
Someday I'll be a regiment
commander and then OSF chief.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.770
You? OSF chief?

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:40.280
The conflict between Suoh
and Seiran isn't over.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:44.110
We need to deepen the ties
between our cities.

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:48.990
And leaders who don't understand
that just get in the way.

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:52.500
I'll continue serving until my
discharge order comes through.

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:56.750
Until then, I'll try to keep
the OSF on the right path.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:59.420
There's nothing to worry about
while you two are here.

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:01.340
Stop by anytime you want.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:04.470
We can even have another gyoza party.

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:08.720
I don't really care either way.
Just don't order so much next time.

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:13.390
A toast to the successful destruction
of the Kunad Gate! Cheers!

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:16.060
Cheers!

00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:19.730
This gyoza really is good,
but you ordered way too much.

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:21.610
We needed it the way you ate.

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:24.650
I don't waste food as
a matter of principle.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:25.990
Did you see Hanabi?

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:27.780
No, not yet.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:32.330
Alice's platoon has patrol duty.
You should catch her before then.

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:35.250
Right. Thanks.

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:44.090
Alice has her own platoon.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:48.220
Hanabi. Tsugumi.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:50.260
Yuito!

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:52.720
Is your family all right?

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:53.970
Well...

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:58.060
As for the inhumane experiments
conducted at the OSF Hospital,

00:05:58.060 --> 00:05:59.440
the hospital's director general,
Yanagi Ichijo...

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:00.810
My parents really didn't know what
my uncle was up to at the hospital.

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:04.690
"Was the government involved?"
"Old OSF Hospital under investigation"

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:04.690
My parents really didn't know what
my uncle was up to at the hospital.

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:08.200
"Was the government involved?"
"Old OSF Hospital under investigation"

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:08.200
They were more worried about me.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:11.700
The Ichijo family is in
for tough times ahead,

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:14.830
but I think it's better this way.

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:17.790
Still, it'll be hard on Commander Alice.

00:06:17.790 --> 00:06:22.790
Yeah, the OSF Hospital's director
general is Alice's older brother.

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:25.260
What about you, Yuito? Are you okay?

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:26.420
Huh?

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:30.220
Chief Sumeragi was removed from office.

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:37.390
After my brother's testimony at the
hearing, he was bound to be sacked.

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:42.440
The Extinction Belt may be gone,
but the Sumeragi family's critics persist.

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:45.940
But we can't keep looking to the past.

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:47.440
I agree.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:52.240
I was scouted before joining the OSF,
but after fighting alongside everyone,

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:56.240
I want to make New Himuka
a better place for everybody.

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:58.790
I really believe that.

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:05.420
The sunlight somehow feels warmer
now that the Extinction Belt is gone.

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:08.300
The flowers and trees are delighted.

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:13.050
I'm going to work hard to make sure
they can live in peace.

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:16.890
Kasane. Yuito.

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:18.640
Are you feeling better?

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:20.270
You've been discharged?

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:21.810
We'll miss you.

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:23.860
Yuito, listen to this!

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:28.570
Major General Fubuki and Commander
Alice are going to tie the knot!

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:32.410
We've been engaged for so many years.

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:35.450
There's no need to make
such a big deal about it.

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:39.330
We're looking forward to the wedding!

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:41.370
I'll make the bridal bouquet.

00:07:41.370 --> 00:07:43.830
We appreciate the enthusiasm, but...

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:48.250
Yeah, I don't think we can hold a
ceremony under the circumstances.

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:50.760
Then let's have one with just us at HQ!

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:51.880
We'll think about it.

00:07:51.880 --> 00:07:55.930
Okay, then. Yuito, Kasane,
we'll see you later.

00:07:57.720 --> 00:08:00.430
Sheesh, what's all the fuss about?

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:02.060
Arashi.

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:04.440
Congrats on your discharge, Yuito.

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:09.110
Then again, I suppose it's a weight
off my shoulders, too.

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:13.530
Could it be you're actually still
worried about the major general?

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:18.120
I don't have the energy to
waste on such trivial matters.

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:24.670
Congrats on your promotion
to regiment commander.

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:27.540
So you're really leaving the OSF.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:30.550
What do you have planned next?

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:33.090
I'm thinking about going to college.

00:08:33.090 --> 00:08:35.550
There's so much I want to learn.

00:08:35.550 --> 00:08:37.050
I see.

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:40.770
There's a lot I want to do, too.

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:46.150
I want to serve the OSF and work toward
changing this nation for the better.

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:48.690
Change it? How?

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:53.110
I want it to be a place where
being a dud isn't a disability.

00:08:53.110 --> 00:08:57.490
Right now, almost no thought
is given to their lives.

00:08:57.490 --> 00:09:00.290
It's as if they don't even exist.

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:02.290
Without psionic power,

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:05.580
they can't even see Visions.

00:09:05.580 --> 00:09:08.130
I was like that as a child.

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:10.920
The experiments I endured
to develop psionic power

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:13.670
were brutal and unrelenting day after day.

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:15.300
And I was all alone.

00:09:16.840 --> 00:09:17.890
Luka?

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:19.550
What's wrong?

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:20.930
It's nothing.

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:24.850
I just felt as if I'd suffered through
the experiments with someone.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:31.780
And because of him, I was able
to overcome my darkest hours.

00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:36.030
But I can't for the life of me
remember his name.

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:37.490
I see.

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:40.450
Anyway, let's give it our best shot.

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:41.580
Yeah.

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:42.620
And you, Kasane.

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:45.830
I don't know what they have
planned for you.

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:47.870
Don't overdo it.

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:50.670
Yeah, I know.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:05.140
Everyone really has forgotten Karen.

00:10:05.140 --> 00:10:07.640
It's like he never existed.

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:20.030
That was the day history changed.

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:22.080
We did it, Fubuki!

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:24.330
A-Alice?

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:35.300
How come we're the only ones
who remember Karen?

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:39.930
Maybe it's because we were connected
with Yuito and Kasane via SAS.

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:42.760
That made us like a Red Strings user.

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:47.310
We could observe what was
happening in our world.

00:10:47.310 --> 00:10:52.020
Yuito, are you sure you're all right?

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:53.650
No need to worry.

00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:57.570
I haven't had any more headaches,
and my psionic power is doing great.

00:10:57.570 --> 00:11:00.280
Is it because the Kunad Gate vanished?

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:02.530
Whatever it is, I'm glad.

00:11:02.530 --> 00:11:04.120
Yeah.

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:08.160
That's great. Keep it up.

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:10.370
Hanabi, press harder.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:11.920
Yes, ma'am!

00:11:11.920 --> 00:11:15.750
I still can't get used to
the fact that Alice is back.

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:17.460
What are you talking about?

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:19.590
She's always been here since we enlisted.

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:20.470
What?

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:23.760
We're in different platoons, but...

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:26.010
Has she always been here?

00:11:27.390 --> 00:11:28.930
W-Wait a sec...

00:11:28.930 --> 00:11:31.520
What were we talking about?

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:39.190
You said there must be
a cause-and-effect link

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:42.780
between Karen's time travel
and Alice's return.

00:11:42.780 --> 00:11:44.990
Have you learned anything else?

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:49.080
It's basically like a ginormous
butterfly effect.

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:51.120
But it's impossible to prove.

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:55.380
So he performed a miracle by
swapping his existence for hers.

00:11:57.590 --> 00:12:00.380
Who performed a miracle?

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:01.930
Karen!

00:12:01.930 --> 00:12:03.260
Karen?

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:06.720
Oh, right.

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:09.180
It's that sort of thing.

00:12:09.180 --> 00:12:13.190
But I can't say I'm a fan
of illogical semantics.

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:19.230
It looks like everyone's forgetting
that Karen ever existed.

00:12:19.230 --> 00:12:21.820
Yeah, it does.

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:23.660
It won't be long before...

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:25.990
Yuito?

00:12:25.990 --> 00:12:26.990
Yuito?

00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:29.200
Yuito!

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:38.340
Everybody but us ended up
forgetting about Karen.

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:41.880
This is the world he wanted.

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:47.800
It's the same as before,
except Alice is alive and Karen is gone.

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:52.560
Still, I think what Karen did was wrong.

00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:57.190
No one should be allowed to alter
history for the sake of someone.

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:02.190
The world has changed.

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:05.910
But this is where we must live.

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:07.530
Yeah.

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:10.870
Karen may have written this new history.

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:12.410
However...

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:16.040
...we're the ones who
will forge a new future.

00:13:16.040 --> 00:13:18.130
That's true.

00:13:18.130 --> 00:13:21.420
It's our future.

00:13:27.260 --> 00:13:28.510
Here you are.

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:29.850
Thanks.

00:13:37.770 --> 00:13:39.190
Fubuki?

00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:42.730
Who's that one for?

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:44.530
Huh?

00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:55.830
Kasane, you're still enlisted
with the OSF, right?

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:59.250
Yeah, until my next post is ready for me.

00:13:59.250 --> 00:14:02.750
Well, if it isn't the hero
who saved the country.

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:05.880
Or is it a rebel we have here?

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:07.880
Kagero. Kyoka.

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:10.260
You're looking well, Yuito.

00:14:11.390 --> 00:14:15.100
I heard you two will take part in
the Lunar Surface Survey project.

00:14:15.100 --> 00:14:18.560
Yes, at the request of
the New Himukan government.

00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:21.820
We'll also help dismantle
the Togetsu faith.

00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:26.860
When BABE shut down,
so did the cold sleep system.

00:14:26.860 --> 00:14:30.570
All the slumbering immigrants
awakened from their capsules.

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:34.790
But I suppose they're no longer
a threat without BABE.

00:14:34.790 --> 00:14:39.290
The government has purged its
records of you two ever being spies.

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:41.880
Give-and-take, a little game adults play.

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:46.300
It shows how much the government
really wants to pick your brains.

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:52.600
Yes, if anything I know might be useful,
I intend to do whatever I can to help.

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:55.970
Yuito, about your father...

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:57.810
What about him?

00:14:57.810 --> 00:15:02.400
Chairman Sumeragi committed
crimes against humanity.

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:06.820
But he was trying to protect
New Himuka from Togetsu.

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:09.570
I plan on emphasizing that fact, as well.

00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:11.660
Thanks, Kyoka.

00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:15.830
What will you do, Kagero,
once the project is well on track?

00:15:15.830 --> 00:15:17.250
What do you mean?

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:21.370
Will you return to the moon if you can?

00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:24.540
My desire to do so vanished ages ago.

00:15:24.540 --> 00:15:27.210
Are you saying nothing
is left for you there?

00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:34.970
I'm curious about what became of my family
and what the Moon is like these days.

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:39.680
But whether I'll be allowed
to go hasn't been decided yet.

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:42.230
I'm sure they'll let you, if you help us.

00:15:42.230 --> 00:15:46.230
Plus, you were commander in chief
of the immigrant group's military,

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:48.440
weren't you, General Shin Daniel?

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:50.280
I told you not to call me that!

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:53.070
That's your real name, right?

00:15:53.070 --> 00:15:56.370
We're counting on you, General.

00:15:56.370 --> 00:15:58.750
Those old-timers plague me to this day.

00:15:58.750 --> 00:16:00.960
They left a data trail a mile wide.

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:02.080
What was that, General?

00:16:02.080 --> 00:16:04.040
Never mind!

00:16:43.620 --> 00:16:46.040
What's the matter, Hanabi?

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:48.960
Yuito's psionic power will...

00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:51.300
It will never be the same.

00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:54.380
If only we'd stopped him that day.

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:56.340
He wouldn't have listened.

00:16:56.340 --> 00:16:58.560
But without Yuito, we'd now be--

00:16:58.560 --> 00:17:00.430
Don't you think I know that?!

00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:03.390
But Kasane will never change.

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:05.690
What the hell is she thinking?!

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:10.280
Are you really gonna go to the moon?

00:17:10.280 --> 00:17:12.610
Yes, I am.

00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:15.450
I'm worried about Kasane, too.

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:18.200
Is she really going to the moon?

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:22.160
The immigrant group's data
and tech still remain in Togetsu.

00:17:22.160 --> 00:17:24.710
If she were to use that...

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:27.670
Who knows what the Moon's like now?

00:17:27.670 --> 00:17:31.880
Worst case scenario,
it's been overrun with Others.

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:35.220
And yet, Kasane still wants to go.

00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:38.090
But why all by herself?

00:17:38.090 --> 00:17:41.350
I hear you joined the Recon Team.

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:46.060
We don't know the situation on the moon,
so I'll head there first, alone.

00:17:46.060 --> 00:17:49.060
You could send an autonomous
observation drone.

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:50.650
There's no need for you--

00:17:50.650 --> 00:17:54.320
What if there are people
under attack by Others?

00:17:54.320 --> 00:17:57.070
We can't help unless
we send a psionics user.

00:17:57.070 --> 00:17:58.410
So someone has to go.

00:17:58.410 --> 00:17:59.280
But...!

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:00.370
I can't take it!

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:02.080
Huh?

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:04.540
I can't live with any more regrets.

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:08.420
I won't give up if there's even
a small chance of saving people.

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:10.130
I won't!

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:11.250
Kasane.

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:16.420
I knew what might happen to you.
I saw it coming.

00:18:16.420 --> 00:18:18.840
Yet, I still had you fight alongside me.

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:20.890
I made you bear the burden.

00:18:20.890 --> 00:18:23.850
I... I made you...

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:28.690
I, too, have regrets.

00:18:28.690 --> 00:18:31.770
That's right! Terrible regrets!

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:34.230
I made a promise to Nagi.

00:18:34.230 --> 00:18:38.740
I said I'd be an amazing OSF member.

00:18:38.740 --> 00:18:40.160
But...

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:41.570
Look at me now.

00:18:41.570 --> 00:18:43.450
Yuito...

00:18:43.450 --> 00:18:46.960
I'm so sorry. I...

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:49.540
I don't want regrets, either.

00:18:49.540 --> 00:18:51.380
So I made up my mind.

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:54.250
I'm going into politics.

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:55.510
What?

00:18:55.510 --> 00:18:58.010
I want to help forge a world where

00:18:58.010 --> 00:19:01.090
the government doesn't
lie or spy on people.

00:19:01.090 --> 00:19:06.220
I also want to advocate for duds and
conduct research on Other Particles.

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:09.100
Even though the Extinction Belt is gone?

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:13.400
Maybe we can reverse the metamorphosis
of those who turned into Others.

00:19:13.400 --> 00:19:14.770
Yuito...

00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:18.740
I'll become a politician
and forge a new future.

00:19:18.740 --> 00:19:23.120
There's no reason the OSF
can't do better as an organization.

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:25.990
People should be allowed
to resign if they want.

00:19:25.990 --> 00:19:29.120
Even so, you're gonna stay put,
right, Shiden?

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:30.620
Of course, I am.

00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:33.000
At least till you become OSF chief?

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:34.500
That's irrelevant.

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:36.920
I don't know how far I'll make it.

00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:38.300
Nevertheless, I will...

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:39.470
Same here.

00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:41.970
Who knows how long my body will hold out?

00:19:41.970 --> 00:19:44.850
But I plan to keep fighting while I can.

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:49.980
We're not much different from Kasane
and her little lunar adventure.

00:19:50.980 --> 00:19:54.060
I'm sure Yuito has big plans, too.

00:19:54.060 --> 00:19:57.980
He's not the type that
willingly fades into obscurity.

00:19:57.980 --> 00:20:01.240
I bet he's gonna enter politics.

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:04.910
We'll have to work hard to
keep up with Yuito and Kasane.

00:20:04.910 --> 00:20:08.040
It's hard to imagine
that naive kid in politics.

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:11.670
You'll have to give him
some pointers, General.

00:20:11.670 --> 00:20:15.000
Yeah! You should become his mentor!

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:16.800
What do you say, General?

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:20.010
I think it's a wonderful idea, General.

00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:23.130
Enough already, jeez!

00:20:23.130 --> 00:20:27.510
It's time for me to go. Duty calls.

00:20:27.510 --> 00:20:29.770
That's just like you.

00:20:29.770 --> 00:20:33.560
A politician, huh?
That's right up your alley.

00:20:33.560 --> 00:20:36.730
Honestly, I wasn't sure.

00:20:36.730 --> 00:20:38.860
But I've made up my mind.

00:20:38.860 --> 00:20:40.990
Thank you, Kasane.

00:20:40.990 --> 00:20:43.820
For what?

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:47.120
Truth be told, I worried at first.

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:51.790
But even though we're going it alone,
we're all doing the best we can.

00:20:51.790 --> 00:20:54.870
If we look at it that way, then surely...

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:57.130
I want to change the world,

00:20:57.130 --> 00:21:00.800
although that may sound like hyperbole.

00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:05.050
We saved the world,
so who's to say we can't change it?

00:21:05.050 --> 00:21:08.600
So it's college for me,
and the moon for you.

00:21:08.600 --> 00:21:13.730
Though a vast distance will separate us,
we'll still be in the same world.

00:21:13.730 --> 00:21:15.940
I'll leave the earth in your hands.

00:21:15.940 --> 00:21:18.400
You can count on me.

00:21:18.400 --> 00:21:21.740
I want to live in the here and now.

00:21:24.320 --> 00:21:26.530
Others sighted in District E-24!

00:21:26.530 --> 00:21:27.450
Haruka.

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:29.830
Alice Platoon, deploy there ASAP!

00:21:31.750 --> 00:21:33.830
Shiden Platoon!
You have orders to move out!

00:21:33.830 --> 00:21:35.750
Okay, people, let's go!

00:21:35.750 --> 00:21:37.210
I'll join you.

00:21:37.210 --> 00:21:39.000
You're going, too?

00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:41.670
I'm still a member of the OSF!

00:21:43.970 --> 00:21:47.640
We are always alone, every one of us.

00:21:50.760 --> 00:21:55.350
Though we may be alone,
we're still connected.

00:21:55.350 --> 00:21:58.730
There's always someone there for us.

00:22:04.190 --> 00:22:05.900
"From: Yuito Sumeragi"

00:22:18.500 --> 00:22:21.040
Though we may be far apart...

00:22:28.220 --> 00:22:31.680
Even though we can't see each other...

00:22:33.600 --> 00:22:35.230
...our ties bind us.

00:22:49.030 --> 00:22:56.870
<i>I've been a prisoner</i>
<i>of my own longing</i>

00:22:58.670 --> 00:23:06.460
<i>The shimmering heat signals me to halt</i>

00:23:06.460 --> 00:23:08.590
<i>There's a stranger in me</i>

00:23:08.590 --> 00:23:11.090
<i>I'll fly high so I won't be scared</i>

00:23:11.090 --> 00:23:16.350
<i>By this new self I've never seen</i>

00:23:16.350 --> 00:23:18.140
<i>I'm spreading my wings</i>

00:23:18.140 --> 00:23:20.480
<i>Bird in florid flight</i>

00:23:20.480 --> 00:23:25.190
<i>Lift your eyes to the scarlet sky</i>

00:23:25.190 --> 00:23:30.410
<i>Overtaken by the mighty wind</i>

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:35.580
<i>The view unfolds upon a world</i>
<i>that begins turning</i>

00:23:35.580 --> 00:23:40.040
<i>Amid the intermingling light</i>

00:23:40.040 --> 00:23:45.920
<i>I keep searching for tomorrow</i>

00:23:45.920 --> 00:23:47.550
<i>Tomorrow's in your hands</i>

00:23:47.550 --> 00:23:50.760
<i>Don't tell me now you're afraid</i>

00:23:50.760 --> 00:23:52.390
<i>There's no time to waste</i>

00:23:52.390 --> 00:23:55.350
<i>Keep going forward</i>

00:23:55.350 --> 00:23:59.680
<i>There's nothing to be afraid of</i>

00:23:59.680 --> 00:24:01.350
<i>Now, let's go</i>

00:24:01.350 --> 00:24:06.820
<i>Into a brand-new day</i>
